{"name":"Gainsboro","hex":"#dcdcdc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gainsboro","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A neutral light grey colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a neutral light grey colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gainsboro"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gainsborough, Ipswich","blocks":[{"text":"Gainsborough is an area of Ipswich, in the Ipswich district, in the county of Suffolk, England. It was named after the artist Thomas Gainsborough of Sudbury, who lived in Ipswich for several years. He was noted for visiting the banks of the Orwell in this area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Ipswich_Golden_Hind.jpg/330px-Ipswich_Golden_Hind.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gainsborough%2C_Ipswich","wikidata":"Q2136645"},{"title":"Gainsborough Ward, Ipswich","blocks":[{"text":"Gainsborough Ward is a ward in the South East Area of Ipswich, Suffolk, England. It returns three councillors to Ipswich Borough Council."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Map_Gainsborough_Ward%2C_Ipswich.png/330px-Map_Gainsborough_Ward%2C_Ipswich.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gainsborough_Ward%2C_Ipswich","wikidata":"Q71951624"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Gainsborough%27s_new_library_under_construction_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1097520.jpg/120px-Gainsborough%27s_new_library_under_construction_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1097520.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Gainsborough%27s_new_library_under_construction_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1097520.jpg/250px-Gainsborough%27s_new_library_under_construction_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1097520.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig